  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1135 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nHeat continues to be the primary concern with the upper-level high \nthat extends from the Southern Plains into the Mississippi and Ohio \nRiver Valleys. This pattern will remain mostly unchanged through the \nweek with the high moving slightly eastward Wednesday into Thursday \nbefore moving back to the west over the Great Plains by the end of \nthis week. As a result, there will not be much relief from the \nheat as highs remain in the mid to upper 90s and overnight lows \nonly drop down into the mid to upper 70s. Southerly flow into \nthe region will bring increasing moisture as the week goes on \nsupporting heat index values between 100 and 105 with the \ngreatest chance (15-25%) of reaching 105 on Friday afternoon for\nareas south of I-70. Northern MO could see some relief from the\nheat as high pressure moves back west this weekend and \nshortwaves along the eastern edge of the ridge could trigger \nsome convection.",
